From 66f930959071e7b648b3126c18ca2bf3eac06def Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Carlos Cueto <crcueto25@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 07:00:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] D2: a DuDe BPC releases its kids

PATCH(dude-2). c_dude::decompose_bridge creates the kids of a BPC with
new c_BPC and addKid(); reorganize_kids_f/insert2tree keep each in
exactly one parent's m_kids. ~c_dude deletes only the root BPCs
(m_bpcs) and ~c_BPC was empty, so every kid leaked (100 blocks of 184 B
in the H-03 test). ~c_BPC now deletes its kids; no c_BPC is copied.
LeakSanitizer, H-03 test alone: 1,808,000 B / 11,650 allocations before,
1,789,600 B / 11,550 after (Direct 24,000 -> 5,600). DudeReference
unchanged (own process and whole program); no ASan or UBSan report.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/bpc.cpp | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/bpc.cpp b/src/bpc.cpp
index cf8aa85..a2b4eac 100644
--- a/src/bpc.cpp
+++ b/src/bpc.cpp
@@ -18,7 +18,13 @@ c_BPC::c_BPC() {
   m_pre = NULL;
 }
 
-c_BPC::~c_BPC() { int a = 1; }
+c_BPC::~c_BPC() {
+  int a = 1;
+  // PATCH(dude-2): a BPC owns its kids (decompose_bridge creates them with
+  // new; insert2tree keeps each in exactly one m_kids); they were never freed
+  for (list<c_BPC *>::iterator i = m_kids.begin(); i != m_kids.end(); i++)
+    delete *i;
+}
 
